.TH ENCLO 1 "2026-06-07" "enclo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
enclo \- modular rootless container launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B enclo
[\fB\-c\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B enclo
manages Podman containers using a declarative set of pluggable security modules.
Each module contributes environment variables, volume mounts, and podman arguments
before the container starts. Modules that require sidecar processes (secrets
service, D-Bus proxy) are started alongside the container and torn down when it
exits.
.PP
Container configs live at
.IR ~/.config/enclo/containers/<NAME>.toml .
Pass
.B \-\-config
to override the name-based lookup.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Explicit path to a container config file. Overrides the default lookup at
.IR ~/.config/enclo/containers/<NAME>.toml .
.SH COMMANDS
.SS serve
Start the enclo daemon.
.PP
.B enclo serve
.PP
On Linux, registers a D-Bus session service at
.BR org.enclo.Manager .
On macOS, listens on a Unix socket at
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/enclo/daemon.sock .
A running daemon is replaced. Usually managed by the
.BR enclo.service (5)
systemd user unit.
.SS run
Start a container directly, in the foreground, without a daemon.
.PP
.B enclo run
[\fINAME\fR]
.PP
Orchestrates all enabled modules, starts the container, and blocks until the
container exits.
.IR NAME
defaults to
.BR default .
.SS start
Ask the daemon to start a container.
.PP
.B enclo start
[\fINAME\fR]
.PP
.IR NAME
defaults to
.BR default .
.SS stop
Ask the daemon to stop a container.
.PP
.B enclo stop
[\fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
.TP
.B \-\-force
Stop even if there are active
.BR podman-exec (1)
sessions attached to the container.
.PP
Without
.BR \-\-force ,
the command fails if any exec sessions are open.
.IR NAME
defaults to
.BR default .
.SS restart
Ask the daemon to stop then start a container.
.PP
.B enclo restart
[\fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
.TP
.B \-\-force
Restart even if there are active exec sessions.
.PP
.IR NAME
defaults to
.BR default .
.SS enter
Enter a running container, starting it via the daemon first if necessary.
.PP
.B enclo enter
[\fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-\fR \fICMD\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]]
.PP
.IR NAME
defaults to
.BR default .
.I CMD
defaults to the
.B exec_shell
from the container config (default:
.BR bash ).
.PP
If the container is not running, the daemon is asked to start it before execing in.
The working directory inside the container defaults to the current directory on the
host, or
.B exec_workdir
from the config if set.
.SS exec
Exec into an already-running container without contacting the daemon.
.PP
.B enclo exec
[\fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-\fR \fICMD\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]]
.PP
Errors if the container is not running. Does not attempt to start it.
.IR NAME
defaults to
.BR default .
.I CMD
defaults to
.B exec_shell
from config.
.SS reload
Send SIGHUP to the modules of a running container that support hot-reload.
.PP
.B enclo reload
[\fINAME\fR]
.PP
Currently reloads the secrets service (re-reads store config and proxy rules).
The container is not restarted.
.IR NAME
defaults to
.BR default .
.SS status
Show container status.
.PP
.B enclo status
[\fINAME\fR]
.PP
With no
.IR NAME ,
lists all known containers and their states. With a name, shows detailed
status including module health.
.SS setup-volume
Create missing directories inside the home named volume with correct ownership.
.PP
.B enclo setup-volume
[\fINAME\fR]
[\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print what would be created without making any changes.
.PP
.IR NAME
defaults to
.BR default .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/enclo/containers/<NAME>.toml
Container config file (Linux).
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/enclo/containers/<NAME>.toml
Container config file (macOS).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/enclo/<name>/
Per-container runtime state: module sockets, exec-env file.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/enclo/daemon.sock
Daemon socket (macOS).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Start the daemon (usually done by systemd)
enclo serve

# Start a container via the daemon
enclo start dev

# Open a shell in the container
enclo enter dev

# Run a one-off command without starting via daemon
enclo exec dev -- git status

# Reload secrets config without restarting
enclo reload dev

# Check container status
enclo status
enclo status dev

# Stop the container
enclo stop dev

# Force-stop (ignores open exec sessions)
enclo stop dev --force

# Run a container directly (no daemon, blocks)
enclo run dev

# Use an explicit config file
enclo --config ~/my-container.toml run
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR enclo-container (1),
.BR podman (1),
.BR podman-run (1),
.BR xdg-dbus-proxy (1),
.BR gpg-agent (1)
.PP
Full documentation:
.I docs/configuration.md
and
.I docs/commands.md
in the enclo source tree.
